<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Soporcel posts H1 profit after loss.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Soporcel posts H1 profit after loss.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 to June 30:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Net 2.8 vs 1.0 loss</p>
<p>Operating result 3.9 vs 0.4</p>
<p>Financial result 1.2 loss vs 1.6 loss</p>
<p>Turnover 33.9 vs 30.4</p>
<p>Cash flow 9.7 vs 5.8</p>
<p>Volumes sold (tonnes) 280,000 vs 251,000 Debt 36.7 vs 52.5 NOTE: Full company name is Soporcel-Sociedade Portuguesa de Celulose, S.A., a Portuguese paper and pulp company. The quantities sold of pulp and paper were 280,000 tonnes in the first half 1997, up from 251,000 in the same year-ago period, as the company's paper and pulp factories improved their operational efficiency, Soporcel said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
